# FinnOS base image — aarch64, the ARM dev machine.
#
# One package per line, as mkarchiso reads it; base/setup.sh reads the same
# file. This follows the shared base with the ARM kernel, no x86 microcode,
# and no Wine runtime (Arch Linux ARM does not package Wine for aarch64, so
# naming it here would be a list that does not resolve).
#
# ARM boots through UEFI only, and it gets firmware from linux-firmware plus
# whatever the board ships in its own boot chain. The audio and Bluetooth
# packages are the same ones the x86_64 image carries, and they exist in
# the Arch Linux ARM repositories; the 32-bit GL/Vulkan stack does not, and
# neither does Wine, so neither is named.

# The init system and the shell the disc boots into.
base
systemd
systemd-sysvcompat
sudo
util-linux
kbd

# The kernel, its firmware and the DRM/KMS stack the compositor drives.
linux-aarch64
linux-firmware
libdrm
libinput
seatd

# Mesa provides the GBM and EGL the accelerated path uses; libglvnd is the
# dispatch pkg-config's egl and glesv2 look for. Mesa's own dependencies
# name the `wayland` client library; it is not what pacman.conf refuses
# (that is the compositors), and this is why.
mesa
libglvnd
wayland
wayland-protocols
libxkbcommon

# What finn-comp links against.
freetype2
fontconfig
libwebp
alsa-lib
alsa-ucm-conf
ttf-dejavu

# Audio and Bluetooth: the same set the x86_64 profile carries, because the
# shell's Control Center shows the same tiles and the packages exist for
# ARM. There is no Vulkan driver for the ARM VM's emulated GPU, so none is
# named; a machine that has one can add it.
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
bluez
bluez-utils

# NetworkManager configures connections; wpa_supplicant provides Wi-Fi.
networkmanager
wpa_supplicant
openssh
curl

# Linux desktop apps use Flatpak; setup.sh initializes the system Flathub.
flatpak

# jq and zstd, as on x86_64: finnpkg's winget path parses JSON with jq, and
# zstd is what pacman and the live squashfs use.
jq
zstd

# The installer and the tools it needs.
arch-install-scripts
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
parted
gptfdisk

# GRUB is the bootloader on an ARM board; there is no syslinux and no BIOS
# boot partition there. The tools the machine that writes the disc needs
# are not on it: see "Building the medium" in README.md.
grub
efibootmgr

# Python for FinnSDK and the shell's tooling; git and the compiler because
# the machine builds the compositor from the sources the disc carries.
python
git
nano
vim
base-devel
pkgconf
# The local packages in base/pkgbuilds are deliberately not in this list:
# nothing on the disc installs from a repository that does not exist. The
# compositor and the SDK are built by the machine, from the sources.
